# Merge to main needs approval

Agents **may** commit and **may** `git push -u origin <feature-branch>` after the merge-ready gate.

Agents **must not** land work on `main` until the user approves. Approval is **not** a second round-trip after they already said the close-out words.

## What counts as approval

Any of these in this conversation, for the **current** merge-ready ship:

- **CMPH** — standing close-out. Means: print the hitch table, **commit**, **merge to `main`**, **push `origin main`**, write the handoff. Do **not** stop to ask “merge?” again.
- “merge to main”, “land it”, “ship to main”, “commit MERGE push handoff”

Docs-only / rules-only slices have **no** Tier 2 smoke. Do not invent a smoke wait. Deployable DLL ships still need smoke **PASS** (or an explicit waive) before that merge ([deploy-before-smoke.mdc](deploy-before-smoke.mdc)).

## Forbidden without that approval

- `git checkout main` + merge or rebase of the story
- `git push origin main` (or any push that updates `main`)
- Deleting the feature branch as if it were already merged
- Opening a PR unless the user asked for one

## After pushing the feature branch

If they already said **CMPH** / MERGE / land: merge, push `main`, delete the feature branch, handoff. **Do not** ask again.

If they have **not** said any of those: stop, summarize, ask. Waiting on that answer is a **pause** — do not start the next PM story ([one-story-one-ship.mdc](one-story-one-ship.mdc)).

## After the user approves

Then follow [AGENT_HANDOFF.md](../../AGENT_HANDOFF.md) → *Git workflow*: merge locally to `main`, push `origin main`, delete the feature branch (local + remote).
